        {q:'A suspect’s phone connects to a cell tower covering a large district. What can this alone prove?',opts:['Exact street location','Presence somewhere within an approximate coverage area, subject to network conditions','That the owner committed the offence','That the phone was in the owner’s hand'],a:1,why:'Cell-site data is geographically coarse and does not by itself identify the user.'},
        {q:'A report contains a conclusion that is stronger than its underlying data. What is the best review?',opts:['Accept the author’s seniority','Trace each conclusion to source evidence and narrow unsupported claims','Remove all data','Choose the most dramatic interpretation'],a:1,why:'Conclusions must not exceed what the underlying evidence supports.'}
